From ce2708ddeed3a67ca3252afdec999a2aa5ce9aab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:59:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): paint the sidebar from the stored session
 outcome [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- sessionStatusStripe: row.outcome wins when present (done green, decision red,
  muted grey, waiting/running grey glyph, unresolved amber); a live turn and a
  ⌘B park still beat it; no outcome keeps the old derivation.
- Stripe tooltip from the outcome: summary, open questions, what it waits on,
  or the unresolved reason in words.
- ⌘B writes through POST /api/sessions/{id}/mute and reads row.muted; the
  local list stays as the optimistic cache and as the only record against an
  older backend. A failed POST reverts and toasts.
- kanban_notice rows with display_metadata.stale render dimmed, labelled
  "outdated: card moved on".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
